  "problem": "$\\,$ Read the book, or you won't understand the lecture.\n\nWhich conditional statement is logically equivalent to the disjunctive statement above?",
  "worked_solution": "Let's denote by $A$ and $B$ the following statements:\n\n- $A:$ Read the book.\n\n- $B:$ You won't understand the lecture.\n\nThen, our initial statement can be written as $A\u2228B,$ which is logically equivalent to \n\n$$\n\u00acA\u21d2B.\n$$\n\nThe negation of $A$ can be written as\n\n- $\u00acA:$ You don't read the book.\n\nTherefore, the given statement is logically equivalent to the following:\n\n$\\,$ If you don't read the book, then you won't understand the lecture.",
